  "slug": "heterogeneous-latent-a78a",
  "summary": "Recent preprints show that heterogeneous neural recordings can be aligned and modeled to expose shared latent variables.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these five preprints is the recovery of shared latent structure from neural data that differ in session, subject, or recording format. Neuralign jointly aligns and decomposes heterogeneous recordings into shared tensor components, and Unified CEBRA pools recordings across sessions through a shared label to relate single-neuron contributions to population codes in mouse visual cortex. C3PO learns predictive, interpretable latent variables directly from unsorted, unbinned continuous-time spike trains. A digital twin of freely moving mouse V1 links classical tuning and behavioral gain effects to a general visual code, and in Drosophila, heterogeneous short-term plasticity across Kenyon cell inputs reformats temporal information into an explicit population clock. The studies do not address identical questions; what is new is the treatment of heterogeneity as structure to be modeled rather than noise to be removed.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
